# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# www to apex, 301. Both hostnames serve the full site with a 200, so every
# one of the ~8,700 pages exists at two URLs. Search Console shows Google has
# indexed the www copies (www.slateremote.com/ and www.slateremote.com/en/jobs
# both drew impressions), which splits ranking signals across two hosts and
# spends crawl budget on duplicates.
#
# Canonical tags already point at the apex, so this makes the served response
# agree with what the pages declare. :splat preserves the rest of the path.
#
# NOTE: hostname matching in _redirects is only honoured when the www domain
# is attached to this Pages project. If www resolves through a different
# route, this rule never matches and the duplicate stays live. Verify after
# deploy with:  curl -sSI https://www.slateremote.com/en | head -3
# It must answer 301 with `location: https://slateremote.com/en`. If it still
# answers 200, add a Redirect Rule in the Cloudflare dashboard instead
# (Rules > Redirect Rules: hostname equals www.slateremote.com ->
# https://slateremote.com/${http.request.uri.path}, 301).
https://www.slateremote.com/* https://slateremote.com/:splat 301
